            <ArticleTitle>Meckel's diverticulum enterolith: a rare cause of acute abdomen.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>513-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Meckel's diverticulum (MD) is the most common congenital anomaly of the gastro-intestinal tract. Inflammation, bleeding and obstruction are its main complications. Formation of enterolith is rare. A case of acute abdomen caused by Meckel's diverticulitis with enterolith is reported.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
